# (a) Claude finishes a reply, 20 idle minutes pass, the countdown ends, the conversation is big, so the mod compacts it.
title:   Twenty quiet minutes, then a compact
caption: When Claude finishes a reply, idle-compact starts a 20-minute countdown. Nobody sends a message, the countdown runs out, and the conversation is big enough, so it is compacted into a short summary before you come back.
note:    1 column = 1 minute; the ≈ break skips ten quiet minutes. Both numbers are settings: idleSeconds (1200, which is 20 minutes) and minTokens (120000).
focus:   C
break:   +10 min
term:    Compact — Claude Code replaces the conversation so far with a short summary of it, so the next message has far less to re-read.
term:    Tokens — the units a conversation is measured in; a token is roughly three quarters of a word. 120k is 120,000 tokens.

time           0    5m ≈   20m
claude      -S~E-------≈--------
countdown      [=======≈===F
compaction  -----------≈----C---

legend
S  message sent — you ask, Claude starts  blue
~  Claude working  teal
E  reply done — the countdown starts  teal
=  idle countdown · 20 min  violet
F  time is up — big enough: over 120k tokens  violet
C  compacted — now a short summary  green
